Package: lebesgueFDA
Type: Package
Title: Functional Data Analysis under Send-on-Delta Sampling
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ufuk", "Beyaztas", email = "ufuk.beyaztas@marmara.edu.tr",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5208-4950"))
Description: Estimation and identification for samples of curves recorded by
    send-on-delta (Lebesgue) sampling, under which a curve is stored only when
    it has moved a fixed distance from its last stored value. The package
    computes the records exactly, reconstructs each curve by its held, chord
    or midpoint path, and estimates the mean, the covariance and the
    functional principal components from an exact Gram matrix, without
    quadrature. Under a known Lipschitz bound it gives the sharp envelopes of
    the paths compatible with a record, the closed-form identification width,
    the Chebyshev center and radius of the identified set of means, and
    finite-sample simultaneous bands for the identified mean. Generators for
    the six simulation designs of the accompanying paper are included.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: stats
